 "producer": {
  "repository": "FiberOpticsSDK",
  "path": "docs/programs/universal-reactive-rendering-2026-10-18.md",
  "pin": "dcc5b57c4aed",
  "lines": [
   {
    "line": 3,
    "text": "**Status:** design charter only (2026-10-18), no code or backend switch. **Owner:** FiberOpticsSDK. **Authority:** existing Rust-runtime normative requirements/ADRs outrank this additive charter; cross-program decisions: https://github.com/jehalladay/FiberOpticsResearch/tree/main/docs/research/foa/programs/universal-reactive-rendering-2026-10-18.",
    "sha256": "7f4935317d25786b8df7d0f48889a06a58f9bed84ca4f32ca4931f1aa78d729f"
   },
   {
    "line": 11,
    "text": "The historical Rust migration revision was inspected at a516eba8ba1e4f71382a33f1dadc25322a0e4bee; the connected repository did not expose a live ref called rust-runtime on 2026-10-18. It showed portable workspace members fiber-model/fiber-core/fiber-runtime, native-only fiber-python and replay observers, tests/audits protecting no-ambient-API and no-third-party dependencies, and an incomplete PyO3 graph surface. Before implementation, locate/reconcile actual Rust branch/history, fresh heads and main, and rerun existing gates. This charter neither copies code from that revision nor declares it current.",
    "sha256": "0e7deec88bb296f360cbdb2c7d7506230e6e0d735eead7d8245af282d1939953"
   },
   {
    "line": 15,
    "text": "Retain Cargo wasm_subset classification and policy audit in existing normative files. Portable core owns graph validation, refs, dependency capture, scheduling, propagation, transaction/event records, bridge admission, snapshot semantics and replay after implementation. Host capabilities supply clocks/timers/randomness/spawn; the core never imports DOM, JS or networking. Implement browser-capable artifact/bindings outside portable crates (new nonportable adapter target is allowed with documented manifest classification). Preserve canonical value semantic equality versus content-version relation and their independent oracles.",
    "sha256": "88879f43ca4962315bac27860744ca56f82d9ca3f8a9b46d8793df17e5911782"
   },
   {
    "line": 19,
    "text": "## Proposed interfaces (unshipped)",
    "sha256": "55fdf72356fdb6135b61b1777ea30c3d258e3715cbd0f8faac0eb7d17cb296e8"
   },
   {
    "line": 21,
    "text": "- Versioned WASM ABI: initialize(snapshot, capabilities), applyBatch(typedCommands, expectedEpoch), inspect(publicRefs), subscribe(viewSpec), snapshot() and close(); browser-side opaque handles are runtime-scoped.",
    "sha256": "780f68f310bce8ba538cdc3f2ea1b51d530afe592d9d1015966261891635019e"
   },
   {
    "line": 22,
    "text": "- HostCapabilitySet supplies Clock, Timer, Randomness, Spawner explicitly; real and deterministic fake implementations.",
    "sha256": "7f4c91b202172c46da6aa4311c0af8a6f6505b6e7f352c6a93a2db384c4fb72f"
   },
